    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Authenticate with Lyra account\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  login                       Log in with Jianying desktop app first, or use QR/link URL login.\r\n  relogin                     Log in again and replace the current credential after validation.\r\n  qrcode                      Generate a QR code file or terminal rendering for an\r\n                              authorization URL.\r\n  status                      Show current authentication status\r\n  me                          Show current account profile\r\n  check                       Check whether the current login is usable\r\n  logout                      Log out of current account\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Terminal/manual login: no --no-wait.\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --require-jianying-app\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-code\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --link-url\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --credential-json @/tmp/credential.json\r\n\r\n  # Agent/LLM login: split-flow, then finish after the user replies \"authorized\".\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-code --no-wait\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-token '<qr_token>' --qr-device-id '<qr_device_id>' --device-code '<device_code>' --user-code '<user_code>' --session-handoff '<session_handoff>'\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --link-url --no-wait\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --device-code '<device_code>' --user-code '<user_code>' --session-handoff '<session_handoff>'\r\n\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth status\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth me\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth logout\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  In an Agent/LLM QR flow, render qr_image_markdown as an inline image\r\n  and print the returned fallback link.\r\n  Tell the user they can click the fallback link if the QR expires,\r\n  then ask them to reply \"authorized\" after authorization and run completion_command_args / completion_command yourself.\r\n  Use `lyra-cli auth <subcommand> --help` for more information.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Authenticate with Lyra account\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  login                       Log in with Jianying desktop app first, or use QR/link URL login.\r\n  relogin                     Log in again and replace the current credential after validation.\r\n  qrcode                      Generate a QR code file or terminal rendering for an\r\n                              authorization URL.\r\n  status                      Show current authentication status\r\n  me                          Show current account profile\r\n  check                       Check whether the current login is usable\r\n  logout                      Log out of current account\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Terminal/manual login: no --no-wait.\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --require-jianying-app\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-code\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --link-url\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --credential-json @/tmp/credential.json\r\n\r\n  # Agent/LLM login: split-flow, then finish after the user replies \"authorized\".\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-code --no-wait\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --qr-token '<qr_token>' --qr-device-id '<qr_device_id>' --device-code '<device_code>' --user-code '<user_code>' --session-handoff '<session_handoff>'\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --link-url --no-wait\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth login --device-code '<device_code>' --user-code '<user_code>' --session-handoff '<session_handoff>'\r\n\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth status\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth me\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth logout\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  In an Agent/LLM QR flow, render qr_image_markdown as an inline image\r\n  and print the returned fallback link.\r\n  Tell the user they can click the fallback link if the QR expires,\r\n  then ask them to reply \"authorized\" after authorization and run completion_command_args / completion_command yourself.\r\n  Use `lyra-cli auth <subcommand> --help` for more information.\r\n",
